WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.000
BISM ALLAH, ALRAHMAN, ALRAHIM

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
I seek refuge in God from Satan

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
I have a lot to say.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
I don't know why but it all came to my head.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
And it is very important.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Actually, I had a lot to say and I was anxious to change the schedule.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
So, when we were ahead of the schedule in the morning and Shahnaz was speaking here.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
We decided to change the schedule, right?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
But this is destiny.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
It is destined that I speak now at this time with you, certain people, in this hall, now.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Because when we attempted to change the schedule. What happened?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
We couldn't do it.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
And the rain was only here around the... on the dining hall.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
It was rain here only. The rain and the lightening were only here.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
So, we had to go back to the original schedule because it is destiny that I speak now.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:24.000
When you go to school, and enroll in a course and they find that you are deficient in some information,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
they send you back to school to take some prerequisites.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:39.000
You go and take physics or physical chemistry, and then you find the formulae or formulas

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.000
that how things go, differentiation and integration and funny signs.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
And you don't understand a thing and they say oh you didn't take calculus?

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
You say no. So, they send you back to school, say go take some calculus and come back.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.000
And we are, this is what happened to us.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.000
We were in God's kingdom and some deficiency was discovered in us.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:13.000
And some fellow creatures suggested that we'd be flunk, failed and send them all to hell.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.000
And God said I am gonna send them back to school, give them a textbook

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.000
You see the textbook.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.000
And then they are tested, and if they make it, they can come back.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Go take some calculus and come back.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:43.000
After making this statement, I'm realizing that we are here in school to take some additional courses.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.000
We are receiving a lot of information and we are going from test to test.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:00.000
I want to congratulate you, most of you, for making it

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.000
because you have passed the most difficult test.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:14.000
The most difficult test is to have one of us, a human being like us, claim that he is a messenger of God.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
It's a very difficult test.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.000
And I can see now why God calls them AS-SABEGHOON, those who are the elite of the elite,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.000
السّابقون السّابقون the elite of the elite.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.000
But it's a very difficult test, and I myself went through it. So, I am speaking from experience.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.000
God says they are ثلة من الأولين, many from the first generation.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
We are the first generation.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.000
وَقَلِيلٌ مِنَ الآخِرِينَ and few from the later generations.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
We are the ones who took the difficult test.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:03.000
Many will be jumping on the wagon in the near future and thousand and millions are going to join us in the future,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.000
but they don't deserve as much credit as you.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:16.000
I was staying at Farima and Amir Koleimi's house at San Francisco a couple of months ago.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:25.000
And Farima and Amir, like myself, who grew up with the traditional Islam:

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:32.000
they taught us that Muhammad was the last prophet, the last messenger,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.000
but Farima and Amir passed the test,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.000
and they accepted me as God's messenger. They looked at the evidence,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.000
And they believed me.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:47.000
They actually believed God,

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Because God said لَا يَمَسُّهُ إِلَّا الْمُطَهَّرُون

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:55.000
God said, none can touch this book of mine except those who are worthy of it.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:03.000
And they said since God revealed the miracle of Quran through this man, then he must be, he cannot be a liar.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
And they concluded that God is telling the truth.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.000
It's not as easy as I am telling you now. But it's a difficult test. They passed it very easily.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:17.000
A couple of days later, after I stayed with Farima and Amir,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.000
the neighborhood children came to ask what is that messenger of God.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Because Farima and Amir's children went around saying guess who is sleeping in our house?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.000
For the children, for the new generation-

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:41.000
Now God says He promises الحسنة, the beauty and enjoyment and Heaven for all of the believers,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.000
But Farima and Amir's children cannot get the same credit as Farima and Amir.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.000
These are children. They are growing up. They have no hang-ups.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:59.000
They say... their parents say this is God's messenger and we believe it and for them it's easy.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.000
Can you see the difference?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.000
So, I congratulate you. The test is very difficult.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.000
And I said, I passed it.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
I mean I went through it.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.000
Alhamdulillah, I did pass it because I am like you. We are in the same boat.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
I am required also to believe that Rashad Khalifa is a messenger of God,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.000
and it took me 8 years.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Some of you are probably better than me in that respect. It didn't take you that long, but it took me eight years.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:40.000
And this gives me a chance to make it up to some of my most beloved friends.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Edip, where is Edip?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.000
This man is the most curious creature on earth.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.000
He is very curious. He knows your grandmother's name by now.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:58.000
You might not know that he knows, but he is very curious.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.000
and he comes to me and

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:09.000
I mean he goes to the supermarket and reads all the pamphlets and all the bulletin boards, everything, is very curious.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.000
It doesn't make it easy when he comes to me and says how does the revelation come to you?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Do you see Gabriel?

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.000
What does he tell you? what do you tell him? In what form?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:27.000
And it is very difficult to convey this to him, and I can see the disappointment in his face.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.000
He is very dear to me because he is a believer.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Feroz Karmally is also very curious person.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Batool will tell you that.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.000
Very curious and he asked me the same question.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
And he is, he is very very dear to me, Feroz Karmally

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.000
and the disappointment in his face just breaks my heart.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.000
I don't know how, what to tell him, so I am going to tell you now.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:56.000
I see the disappointment on Edip's face and I see it in Feroz's face.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.000
I don't know if I can satisfy their curiosity or not, but I try.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:07.000
There is a precedent in the Quran, as you know Gabriel appeared to Maryam.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.000
He told her he was Gabriel, but what did she say?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.000
She said, إني أعوذ بالرحمن منك

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.000
I seek refuge in God from you.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.000
إن كنت تقيا

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.000
So, she assumed that he is Satan or an agent of Satan or something bad.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:35.000
And before we jump to any conclusions, I want to set some records straight. Gabriel is a messenger of God.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:41.000
He is the messenger who carries the revelations, he is an angel and God calls him روح الامین

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:48.000
The Honest Bearer of Revelation روح الامین

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:57.000
And he is...we may have human... human visions of Gabriel.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:02.000
and we may convey on him human characteristics.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Like, he may say you're God's messenger. I say get away from me, you are Satan.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.000
We would think that he'll get mad and say I'm telling you you are God's messenger.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:17.000
No, he doesn't. He is very mild

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:23.000
very understanding, very gentle and very respectful.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:32.000
And he never never utters the things that we would utter

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Like I'm telling you you'd better do the announcement or listen.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.000
It is amazing, of course, God gave him certain powers. They see certain things.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.000
and they have a tremendous understanding, the angels do.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:51.000
So, they're really angels. The word angels as we understand it is very fitting.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Now, I went through the test because,

00:09:57.000 --> 00:010:00.000
the way the revelation comes, Feroz and Edip,

00:010:00.000 --> 00:010:16.000
is that when... when God is sending information to us, Gabriel seems to just take over my brain, completely, and nothing else.

00:010:16.000 --> 00:010:21.000
I can do nothing else except deal with the piece of information that is coming.

00:010:21.000 --> 00:010:30.000
So, I stated in the perspective one time that Sura Y.S. (36): verse 3: إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ

00:010:30.000 --> 00:010:38.000
I said it that most assertively Gabriel told me that إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ, verse 3 applies to you. Surely, you are one of the messengers.

00:010:38.000 --> 00:010:47.000
And I tried to avoid that because it's a very... it's a very strong statement.

00:010:47.000 --> 00:010:53.000
And I grew up saying Y.S. (یا سین), I was even told that Y.S. is the name of Muhammad.

00:010:53.000 --> 00:011:00.000
But my brain was taken over and you are one of the messengers.

00:011:00.000 --> 00:011:05.000
I said go away, you are Satan which is what Mary said.

00:011:05.000 --> 00:011:09.000
And then a very mild and very gentle debate will go on.

00:011:09.000 --> 00:011:11.000
Why do you think I'm Satan?

00:011:11.000 --> 00:011:16.000
Didn't you, Didn't you say أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ الرَّجِيمِ

00:011:16.000 --> 00:011:21.000
I will actually say this. I would say أَعُوذُ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ, I seek refuge in God, from Satan the rejected.

00:011:21.000 --> 00:011:28.000
And I would say رَّبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَمَزَٰتِ ٱلشَّيَـٰطِينِ my Lord, I seek refuge in you from the whispers of the devil.

00:011:28.000 --> 00:011:35.000
وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ رَبِّ أَنْ يَحْضُرُونِ and I seek refuge in you, my Lord that they come close to me.

00:011:35.000 --> 00:011:41.000
And the debater will say you said these statements, don't you believe God?

00:011:41.000 --> 00:011:44.000
He protects you.

00:011:44.000 --> 00:011:46.000
I am not Satan.

00:011:46.000 --> 00:011:54.000
And this is, when Maryam said I seek refuge in God from you. She said أعوذ بالرحمن منك

00:011:54.000 --> 00:011:57.000
I seek refuge in the Most Gracious from you

00:011:57.000 --> 00:012:05.000
إن كنت تقيا if this means anything to you. In other words, you'll understand what I'm saying if you are really Gabriel.

00:012:05.000 --> 00:012:09.000
Gabriel appeared to Maryam in the form of a human being.

00:012:09.000 --> 00:012:12.000
This did not happen in my case.

00:012:12.000 --> 00:012:14.000
My case is strictly here.

00:012:14.000 --> 00:012:19.000
So, I dismissed the thought, but then I'm, I'm totally incapacitated.

00:012:19.000 --> 00:012:21.000
As far as thinking is concerned, or doing anything. So, I ignored the thought.

00:012:21.000 --> 00:012:25.000
And then I said, I'm gonna read some Quran.

00:012:25.000 --> 00:012:30.000
Then, I opened the Quran and my brain is taken over. You are one of the messengers.

00:012:30.000 --> 00:012:33.000
Sura Y.S., 3 applies to you.

00:012:33.000 --> 00:012:38.000
So, this is... I hope I satisfied at least some of the curiosity of Edip.

00:012:38.000 --> 00:012:41.000
I know tomorrow he will come up with some other question.

00:012:41.000 --> 00:012:44.000
But it was very difficult.

00:012:44.000 --> 00:012:50.000
I also... I think I need to make a correction, also. I was never asked to make the announcement.

00:012:50.000 --> 00:012:56.000
And I think the way I put it down, I may not have expressed myself.

00:012:56.000 --> 00:013:01.000
I was not, I was never ordered until the time of the announcement,

00:013:01.000 --> 00:013:06.000
and the 8 years before that, I was not ordered, but it was implied.

00:013:06.000 --> 00:013:14.000
Like I said, there is gentleness and mildness and obviously there was destiny. There was a certain time for that announcement.

00:013:14.000 --> 00:013:21.000
But I was just told in this fashion of all the information that you're God's messenger.

00:013:21.000 --> 00:013:30.000
And I went on my many ways, saying I will preach the word of God Alone, the worship of God Alone. We don't need any announcements.

00:013:30.000 --> 00:013:35.000
I said ok. Fine. Ok. I know I'm God's messenger. Fine. Leave me alone. These kind of things.

00:013:35.000 --> 00:013:51.000
And then, in the first conference, Satan wanted to spoil that and jump the gun and do something.

00:013:51.000 --> 00:013:59.000
And Susan Rey kind of let the cat out of the bag on pure speculation.

00:013:59.000 --> 00:014:08.000
And then at that time, because Ismail is here, I am gonna relate his part,

00:014:08.000 --> 00:014:13.000
Kathreen Colton was just telling me that when that happened and there was a big commotion,

00:014:13.000 --> 00:014:25.000
She went in a room and she found Ismail Barakat and Ghasem Ahmad of Malaysia, and Mehri and Mahmood Pirooz conferring about this disaster,

00:014:25.000 --> 00:014:28.000
And Ismail Barakat was pacing the room.

00:014:28.000 --> 00:014:33.000
He was very angry and he made a statement that Kathreen heard.

00:014:33.000 --> 00:014:39.000
Ismail is here and he said I'm gonna ask him point blank if he is God's messenger or not.

00:014:39.000 --> 00:014:47.000
He was whispering, by the way, but Kathreen heard him loud and clear.

00:014:47.000 --> 00:014:53.000
And he was determined to ask me.

00:014:53.000 --> 00:014:58.000
At the same time I was praying very hard. Said please God don't let anybody ask me point blank, are you God's messenger?

00:014:58.000 --> 00:015:03.000
Because I would have told them. I would have said yes at the time.

00:015:03.000 --> 00:015:07.000
Edip: Rashad, I asked you a question but you didn't answer me.

00:015:07.000 --> 00:015:10.000
The messenger: What was that? when?

00:015:10.000 --> 00:015:17.000
Edip: I said your name has been mentioned in Quran 19 times. I said it is significant. What's your idea about this?

00:015:17.000 --> 00:015:21.000
The messenger: That was correspondence, right? So, I didn't answer you. That was easy.

00:015:25.000 --> 00:015:31.000
Then, I was in San Francisco and people were in a lot of turmoil. Many of you were there.

00:015:31.000 --> 00:015:39.000
And here is Ismail Barakat, a hard-headed Egyptian, determined, I mean really determined

00:015:39.000 --> 00:015:40.000
He'd back me up

00:015:40.000 --> 00:015:43.000
To ask me, point-blank are you God's messenger?

00:015:43.000 --> 00:015:49.000
And I was... Kathreen said that she was watching me and I was very quiet.

00:015:49.000 --> 00:015:53.000
What she didn't know, maybe she knows now, that I was praying very hard.

00:015:53.000 --> 00:016:01.000
Please God, don't let anybody ask me that question. I don't need anything like this. I'm gonna preach Your word alone and worship of You Alone.

00:016:01.000 --> 00:016:05.000
And what happened Ismail? I give you two minutes.

00:016:05.000 --> 00:016:09.000
You were determined, yeah.

00:016:09.000 --> 00:016:23.000
And we discussed it with Ghasem Ahmad and we had gone to San Francisco to knock down idols. We didn't know of any new ones,

00:016:23.000 --> 00:016:32.000
you see. So, we looked through the Quran and to us a messenger was one who receives scripture.

00:016:32.000 --> 00:016:34.000
And this guy didn't receive any scripture.

00:016:34.000 --> 00:016:38.000
Not as far as we know and if he says that he's received scripture, he is a liar.

00:016:38.000 --> 00:016:42.000
So, I was determined to ask him point blank and get the thing over with.

00:016:42.000 --> 00:016:47.000
And God is my witness. I couldn't open my mouth to ask that question.

00:016:47.000 --> 00:016:48.000
Thank you, sir.

00:016:58.000 --> 00:017:09.000
later, some time later, Ismail was telling me I can't explain why I was so determined to ask you and what made me. Just I didn't do it.

00:017:09.000 --> 00:017:13.000
So, obviously God answered my prayers.

00:017:13.000 --> 00:017:17.000
And the time went by and I had to make the announcement.

00:017:17.000 --> 00:017:23.000
And I said some of you may be ahead of me because

00:017:23.000 --> 00:017:32.000
I really agonized over that Khutba, the sermon of Friday. How will I tell my friends, brothers and sisters about this announcement?

00:017:32.000 --> 00:017:33.000
How many of them will I lose?

00:017:33.000 --> 00:017:39.000
I love them very much. I wanted them to go with me, Insha Allah to heaven.

00:017:39.000 --> 00:017:42.000
And I dreaded losing any of them.

00:017:42.000 --> 00:017:47.000
So, I, I had a sleepless night.

00:017:47.000 --> 00:017:49.000
Then I go for the Khutba on Friday

00:017:49.000 --> 00:017:53.000
And very eloquently, as eloquently as I can, I delivered the Khutba,

00:017:53.000 --> 00:017:57.000
And I tell them that I'm ordered to announce that I'm God's messenger.

00:017:57.000 --> 00:018:06.000
Then, then I go to Kathreen Colton, for example, and

00:018:06.000 --> 00:018:18.000
Oh, I have to, I have to bring to you my condition at the time. I'm sweating away. What do you think of this Kathreen?

00:018:18.000 --> 00:018:22.000
She said I knew that all along.

00:018:22.000 --> 00:018:25.000
What is the big deal?

00:018:25.000 --> 00:018:29.000
Then, I turned to Mohtasham and Susan and they said what took you so long?

00:018:29.000 --> 00:018:35.000
Here I am... I'm out of breath and sweating away and these guys knew all along.

00:018:35.000 --> 00:018:42.000
The funniest one, I went to Lory also and she said well, so, what's the big deal?

00:018:42.000 --> 00:018:45.000
I'm about to die, have a heart attack or something,

00:018:45.000 --> 00:018:50.000
and all these guys already knew, somehow.

00:018:50.000 --> 00:018:53.000
without announcement, just like I knew without an announcement.

00:018:53.000 --> 00:018:56.000
The funniest one was Ihsan Ramadan. Where is she?

00:018:56.000 --> 00:018:58.000
Where is Ihsan? Raise your hand.

00:018:58.000 --> 00:019:06.000
Ihsan was going to our children saying this man is a messenger of God. I knew he's a messenger of God but does he know?

00:019:06.000 --> 00:019:09.000
I wonder if he knows.

00:019:09.000 --> 00:019:13.000
How can I break this news to him?

00:019:19.000 --> 00:019:21.000
Well, these guys were ahead of me.

00:019:21.000 --> 00:019:24.000
And of course, I told you what my daughter said.

00:019:24.000 --> 00:019:29.000
This is the toughest test.

00:019:29.000 --> 00:019:35.000
It is very tough and I congratulate you. That's why I went into length.

00:019:39.000 --> 00:019:44.000
We also trying to take account of this conference

00:019:44.000 --> 00:019:51.000
and I have lost some of my dearest friends because I was subtle.

00:019:54.000 --> 00:019:57.000
But so I'm not gonna be subtle.

00:019:57.000 --> 00:020:02.000
Mahmood read the verse that says they are merciful among themselves and harsh on the disbelievers.

00:020:02.000 --> 00:020:03.000
I'm going to name names.

00:020:03.000 --> 00:020:06.000
