So, Olivia almost jumped and said what do you mean?

00:020:48.000 --> 00:020:54.000
I said yeah, it's not over yet. Wait till you hear me. So, I may cause a lot of turmoil.

00:021:00.000 --> 00:021:04.000
I need to remember the test.

00:021:04.000 --> 00:021:06.000
Yes, the test is very difficult

00:021:06.000 --> 00:021:15.000
but If the person is not a believer, it is amazing how flimsy the test can be and they flunk.

00:021:15.000 --> 00:021:18.000
And this happened to some of my dearest friends

00:021:18.000 --> 00:021:25.000
because inside their heart, they were not disbelieve... they were not believers.

00:021:27.000 --> 00:021:32.000
Flimsy, by flimsy, I give you an example. This is not what happened, but it is an example.

00:021:32.000 --> 00:021:43.000
They will come to the masjid. They will look at the miracle. They will the translation. They will discuss the matter with me. They say worshiping God alone is reasonable. This is what we believe.

00:021:43.000 --> 00:021:46.000
Following the words of God is fine, it is what we believe.

00:021:46.000 --> 00:021:51.000
Then, they go out and a block away, they meet somebody who tells them guess what?

00:021:51.000 --> 00:021:53.000
Rashad Khalifa picks his nose.

00:021:53.000 --> 00:022:04.000
They say he does?! I will never go there again!

00:022:04.000 --> 00:022:06.000
That's how flimsy the test can be.

00:022:06.000 --> 00:022:09.000
Yeah.

00:022:09.000 --> 00:022:17.000
I mean here, I've given, shown them the miracle that God revealed throughout... through us the believers, a whole bunch of us,

00:022:17.000 --> 00:022:21.000
and then for a flimsy reason, they would flunk the test.

00:022:21.000 --> 00:022:28.000
It's a very difficult test, but then it reflects their belief or disbelief inside.

00:022:28.000 --> 00:022:34.000
We had many people come to the mosque, to the Masjid Tucson.

00:022:34.000 --> 00:022:40.000
They'd come to the Quranic studies. They'd come to the Friday prayers, and they would be seemingly good believers.

00:022:40.000 --> 00:022:42.000
Now, this is what actually happens.

00:022:42.000 --> 00:022:48.000
And then, of course, they have to be tested.

00:022:48.000 --> 00:022:55.000
Sura 2....Verse 2 of Sura 29: Do the people think they would be left to say we believe without being put to the test?

00:022:55.000 --> 00:023:02.000
We will surely test them to distinguish the truthful from the liar.

00:023:02.000 --> 00:023:06.000
They have to be tested and it is in my best interest.

00:023:06.000 --> 00:023:11.000
But I happen to fall in love with people easily especially when they say, we're believers.

00:023:11.000 --> 00:023:15.000
I was telling you that Edip is very dear to me, Feroz very dear to me.

00:023:15.000 --> 00:023:19.000
And I explained to you this matter of revelation.

00:023:19.000 --> 00:023:27.000
Even though it is really impossible to convey. I want to tell you anything. I want everything to be open. I don't want anything to be mysterious.

00:023:27.000 --> 00:023:30.000
And I don't want you to hesitate.

00:023:30.000 --> 00:023:43.000
If there's anything mysterious, or taboo or something, don't.... there is no taboo and there is no mystery. You come forward and ask.

00:023:43.000 --> 00:023:48.000
But why are they dear to me? It's because they're believers.

00:023:48.000 --> 00:023:55.000
One of the best advantages of being God's messenger is that I get to know the believers through believers.

00:023:58.000 --> 00:024:06.000
It's such an honor because believers are a rare precious commodity. God said so in the Quran.

00:024:06.000 --> 00:024:12.000
God says most people no matter what you do will not believe and most of those who believe will fall in idol worship (12:103-106).

00:024:12.000 --> 00:024:20.000
So, it is in my best interest that people go through the test and the hypocrites are sifted away.

00:024:20.000 --> 00:024:24.000
But like I said I happen to fall in love with these people.

00:024:24.000 --> 00:024:30.000
So, we have these people come to the masjid, appear to be nice, good believers,

00:024:30.000 --> 00:024:32.000
and then the test:

00:024:32.000 --> 00:024:44.000
And Satan sends a man who is very eloquent and very clever, a man who does not do the five prayers, claims to be a muslim

00:024:44.000 --> 00:024:49.000
And as he sips his whiskey. He tells them Rashad Khalifa is bad.

00:024:49.000 --> 00:024:54.000
It's not exactly he picks his nose, but he doesn't keep his word,

00:024:54.000 --> 00:025:00.000
or he scratches his left ear occasionally, some flimsy really.

00:025:00.000 --> 00:025:03.000
and they would say oh, ok. Then, we'll not go to the mosque. OK?

00:025:03.000 --> 00:025:17.000
So, it reflect... it hurts me, but again it explains why I congratulate you for passing the test.

00:025:17.000 --> 00:025:21.000
The most difficult test is the test of messengership.

00:025:29.000 --> 00:025:32.000
I don't wanna miss anything. I wrote some notes very quickly here.

00:025:32.000 --> 00:025:36.000
God says I will divert from my revelations those who are arrogant.

00:025:36.000 --> 00:025:46.000
And the only reason people flunk this very difficult test is ego.

00:025:49.000 --> 00:025:56.000
And God goes out of His way in the Quran and repeats that say I am a human being like you.

00:025:56.000 --> 00:026:00.000
I am a human being like you.

00:026:00.000 --> 00:026:08.000
And you know what you are. You're not perfect, nor is God's messenger whoever he... whoever it is.

00:026:08.000 --> 00:026:12.000
I'm a human being like you. The key word is like you.

00:026:12.000 --> 00:026:19.000
But what is God's messenger? It's a person through whom God is sending information.

00:026:19.000 --> 00:026:32.000
And the messenger himself is required to listen to this information and is required, like you, to look at it and believe it or disbelieve it.

00:026:32.000 --> 00:026:36.000
and it's the same difficulty that you're going through.

00:026:36.000 --> 00:026:42.000
but it is information from God.

00:026:42.000 --> 00:026:47.000
This is why God say مَّن يُطِعِ الرَّسُولَ فَقَدْ أَطَاعَ اللَّهَ whoever obeys the messenger is obeying God.

00:026:47.000 --> 00:026:52.000
This doesn't mean idol-worship

00:026:52.000 --> 00:026:58.000
which is used frequently to flunk some people.

00:026:58.000 --> 00:027:00.000
You're idolizing Rashad.

00:027:00.000 --> 00:027:05.000
We know better than that. We're listening to the information that's coming from God.

00:027:08.000 --> 00:027:13.000
There is another verse that says, فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ it's a very strong verse

00:027:13.000 --> 00:027:14.000
فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ

00:027:14.000 --> 00:027:19.000
God is saying, No, by your Lord, فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ they are not believers.

00:027:19.000 --> 00:027:25.000
حَتَّىٰ يُحَكِّمُوكَ until they ask your judgement.

00:027:25.000 --> 00:027:29.000
فِيمَا شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ in whatever opinions they dispute.

00:027:29.000 --> 00:027:34.000
ثُمَّ لَا يَجِدُوا فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجًا and then, they find no hesitation in them whatsoever, 

00:027:34.000 --> 00:027:38.000
مِمَّا قَضَيْتَ about your judgement.

00:027:38.000 --> 00:027:43.000
وَيُسَلِّمُوا۟ تَسْلِيمًۭا very powerful word: and submit completely.

00:027:47.000 --> 00:027:52.000
This فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ, by your Lord, they are not believers.

